      "worked": "The original equation requires $\\sin\\theta\\ne0$ and $1+\\cos\\theta\\ne0$. Steps 1–5 produce candidates; these must be checked in the original equation.\n\nAt $\\theta=\\pi$,\n$$\\begin{align*}\\sin\\pi&=0\\\\1+\\cos\\pi&=0.\\end{align*}$$\nBoth sides of the original equation are undefined. Step 6 incorrectly includes $\\theta=\\pi$.\n\nThe other two candidates satisfy the original equation:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{\\sin(\\pi/2)}{1+\\cos(\\pi/2)}&=1\\\\\\operatorname{cosec}(\\pi/2)&=1\\\\\\frac{\\sin(3\\pi/2)}{1+\\cos(3\\pi/2)}&=-1\\\\\\operatorname{cosec}(3\\pi/2)&=-1.\\end{align*}$$\nTherefore $\\theta=\\frac{\\pi}{2},\\frac{3\\pi}{2}$.",
